{"_meta":{"ui":{"resourceUri":"ui://agent-cost-analyzer/views.html"},"ui/resourceUri":"ui://agent-cost-analyzer/views.html"},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Use to estimate what planned work on one project (id from list_projects) or repository (key from list_repositories) will cost: a p50\u2013p90 range in USD at today's prices, never a single number, labelled \"estimate\". It is the median and 90th-percentile cost per active day (or per session) in the last 4 or 12 weeks \u00d7 the planned active days (or sessions); days or sessions with any unpriced turn are left out and counted. With fewer than 5 known days or sessions there is no range: `refusal` says why. AI Credits are converted at 1 AI Credit = $0.01. With `model`, it estimates on that model instead: every session of the target in the window is replayed on it (as replay_session does) and the unit costs are the simulated ones, priced on each session's own channel as of when it ran (pricing \"as-of-use\"). Those figures are Simulated (same conversation and token counts assumed); `simulation` gives the method, the sessions and turns replayed, the rest by reason, how many self-checks passed, and the assumptions.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","properties":{"activeDays":{"description":"Planned active days (or give sessions).","maximum":9007199254740991,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"historyWeeks":{"anyOf":[{"const":4,"type":"number"},{"const":12,"type":"number"}],"description":"History window in weeks: 4 or 12 (default)."},"model":{"description":"Estimate on this model instead (a model id a vendor profile lists, e.g. \"claude-haiku-5.5\"): the target's sessions replayed on it, Simulated.","maxLength":100,"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"projectId":{"description":"The project id, from list_projects (or give repository).","minLength":1,"type":"string"},"repository":{"description":"A reposit